# AISO: "Top 1%" Mobile Design & Haptics Checklist

Track our step-by-step progress as we elevate the AISO Capacitor app into the top tier of native experiences.

---

- `[x]` **Phase 1: Native Capacitor Haptics Integration**
  - `[x]` Run `npm install @capacitor/haptics`
  - `[x]` Sync Android native layers via `npx cap sync android`
- `[x]` **Phase 2: GPU Cosmic Aurora & Liquid Background**
  - `[x]` Add low-opacity rotating aura blurs keyframes in `src/app/globals.css`
  - `[x]` Replace `/bg-mountains.png` with dynamic fluid gradients in `src/app/page.tsx`
- `[x]` **Phase 3: Real-Time Agent Packet Pulses**
  - `[x]` Add traveling light-packet animations down connector lines in `AgentTraceCard`
  - `[x]` Apply pulsing radial rings to the active agent node
- `[x]` **Phase 4: Physical Haptic Triggers**
  - `[x]` Set up dynamic client imports for `@capacitor/haptics` in `src/app/page.tsx`
  - `[x]` Trigger Light taps on tabs/buttons, Medium taps on inputs, and Success/Warning vibration strings on results
- `[x]` **Phase 5: Bento Receipts & Accordion History**
  - `[x]` Refactor confirmation receipt with dynamic serrated ticket border shapes (`clip-path` and absolute dividers)
  - `[x]` Refactor past bookings to expand details smoothly in-place in the orders tab
- `[x]` **Phase 6: Compilation & GitHub Push**
  - `[x]` Run `npm run build` to ensure 100% Type-safe compilation
  - `[x]` Stage, commit, and push all final changes to `main` branch
